{#
  The posture block, shared by both reports so the executive summary and the
  technical detail can never disagree about the same organization.
#}
<h2 class="section-title" id="posture">Security posture</h2>

<table class="posture-hero">
  <tr>
    <td class="ring-cell">
      {# `safe` because the ring is built from an integer the chart module
         bounds to 0-100 -- no customer-supplied string reaches it. #}
      {{ report.posture.security_score | score_ring | safe }}
      {% if report.posture.score_delta is not none %}
        <span class="delta">
          {{ '+' if report.posture.score_delta > 0 else '' }}{{ report.posture.score_delta }}
          since the previous reading
        </span>
      {% else %}
        {# Not "no change". There is nothing to compare against, and the two
           mean opposite things to somebody deciding whether remediation is
           working. #}
        <span class="delta delta-none">no earlier reading to compare against</span>
      {% endif %}
    </td>
    <td>
      <p class="eyebrow">Open findings by severity</p>
      {# Bars are drawn against the largest count rather than the total, so
         the longest bar is always full width and the others read against it. #}
      {% set widest = report.posture.by_severity | map(attribute='count') | max %}
      <table class="bars">
        {% for row in report.posture.by_severity %}
        <tr>
          <td class="bar-label"><span class="sev sev-{{ row.severity }}">{{ row.severity | title }}</span></td>
          <td>
            <div class="track">
              {% if row.count and widest %}
              <div class="fill fill-{{ row.severity }}" style="width: {{ (row.count / widest * 100) | round(1) }}%"></div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </td>
          <td class="bar-count">{{ row.count }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<table class="kpis">
  <tr>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ report.posture.asset_count }}</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Assets under assessment</span>
    </div></td>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ report.posture.open_finding_count }}</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Open findings</span>
    </div></td>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ report.posture.verified_resolved_in_window }}</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Verified fixed in the last {{ report.posture.window_days }} days</span>
    </div></td>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ (report.posture.remediation_rate * 100) | round(0) | int }}%</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Share of findings ever raised that are now verified fixed</span>
    </div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

{#
  A finding somebody decided to live with is not a finding that went away.
  Folding accepted risks into "not open" would let a report claim a clean
  environment that is clean by decision rather than by remediation, so the
  count is stated wherever it is not zero.
#}
{% if report.posture.accepted_risk_count %}
<div class="note">
  <p class="note-title">
    {{ report.posture.accepted_risk_count }} open finding{{ '' if report.posture.accepted_risk_count == 1 else 's' }}
    accepted as risk
  </p>
  <p class="small">
    An accepted risk is a decision to live with a finding, not a fix — it is
    excluded from the counts above and is still present in the environment.
  </p>
</div>
{% endif %}

{#
  The shape behind the delta. One number says something moved; the line says
  whether that is a trend or a wobble, which is the difference between a
  customer acting on this report and filing it.

  `safe` because the SVG is built from integers the chart module has already
  bounded to 0-100 -- no customer-supplied string reaches it.
#}
{% set trend = report.posture.history | score_trend %}
{% if trend %}
<div class="card">
  <table class="card-head">
    <tr>
      <td class="card-title">Score trend</td>
      <td class="right small muted">Last {{ report.posture.window_days }} days</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  {{ trend | safe }}
  <p class="small muted">
    Security score across the {{ report.posture.history | length }} reading{{ '' if report.posture.history | length == 1 else 's' }}
    taken in the last {{ report.posture.window_days }} days, on a fixed 0–100 scale.
  </p>
</div>
{% endif %}

<p class="footnote">
  "Verified fixed" means a later scan observed the check passing. CloudGuard
  never closes a finding because somebody said it was fixed.
</p>
